---
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import SupportShell from '../components/SupportShell.astro';
import CategoryIcon from '../components/CategoryIcon.astro';
import ActionIcon from '../components/ActionIcon.astro';
---
<SupportShell title="About JotColoring" description="JotColoring brings the simple joy of a coloring page to the way you create today: on paper, on your screen, and at your own pace." kind="about" eyebrow="LESS RUSH. MORE COLOR.">
 <div slot="hero" class="support-actions"><a class="support-button" href="/coloring-pages/">Find your next page<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a><a class="support-button secondary" href="/studio/">Try Coloring Studio<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></div>
 <section class="support-about-manifesto"><div><p class="support-kicker">WHY JOTCOLORING EXISTS</p><h2>A blank page.<br/>A fresh possibility.</h2></div><div><p>Sometimes you want a quiet few minutes. Sometimes you need an activity for a class, a rainy afternoon or a table full of crayons. Finding a page and starting should feel easy.</p><p>JotColoring was created to bring discovery, printing and browser coloring into one place. Pick a subject that catches your attention, take it to paper or add your first color right here. There is no single right way to finish it.</p></div></section>
 <div class="support-section-heading"><p class="support-kicker">WHAT YOU CAN DO HERE</p><h2>From “that looks fun” to “I made this.”</h2><p>A collection to explore, tools to experiment with, and a space to keep the work you want to return to.</p></div>
 <div class="support-card-grid support-about-steps"><section class="support-card"><CategoryIcon name="animals" size={70}/><h2>Follow your curiosity.</h2><p>Explore animals, flowers, fantasy, patterns and more. Search a subject, narrow your choices and preview a page before you decide.</p><a href="/coloring-pages/">Explore coloring pages<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section><section class="support-card"><ActionIcon name="pdf"/><h2>Take it to paper.</h2><p>Download an uncolored PDF or image and make room for pencils, markers or crayons. The public drawing stays black and white, ready for your own colors.</p><a href="/printing-guide/">Get printing tips<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section><section class="support-card"><ActionIcon name="brush"/><h2>Make the screen your canvas.</h2><p>Use the browser Studio to fill regions, draw, work with layers, add text and place colorable objects. Save a project locally and return when inspiration does.</p><a href="/studio/">Open Coloring Studio<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section></div>
 <section class="support-about-banner"><div><p class="support-kicker">A COLLECTION THAT BECOMES YOUR OWN</p><h2>Keep the pages. Keep the possibilities.</h2><p>My Artwork gives saved projects and favorite pages a home in this browser. Organize them into boards, add notes and tags, track your progress, and download a portable backup. Your next creative moment can start where you left off.</p><div class="support-actions"><a class="support-button secondary" href="/my-artwork/">Visit My Artwork<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></div></div><CategoryIcon name="flowers" size={105}/></section>
 <div class="support-card-grid"><section class="support-card"><CategoryIcon name="fantasy" size={70}/><h2>Start with your imagination.</h2><p>Create with AI can turn a written idea into a new page when generation is available. Photo to Coloring Page creates outlines from your photo on your device. Compare the result and adjust the detail before downloading or coloring it. Each tool has its own space, separate from Studio.</p><a href="/create/photo/">Explore Photo to Coloring Page<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section><section class="support-card"><CategoryIcon name="mandalas" size={70}/><h2>Examples inspire, you decide.</h2><p>Half-colored examples show one way a page might look. They are a starting point for imagination. Public collection downloads contain uncolored outlines with a small JotColoring brand credit.</p><a href="/coloring-pages/mandalas/">Find a pattern to color<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section><section class="support-card"><ActionIcon name="heart"/><h2>Enjoy it with clear permission.</h2><p>Personal and non-commercial educational use is free. Commercial projects need written permission. We explain the difference so you can choose the right use with confidence.</p><a href="/license/">Read the artwork license<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section></div>
 <div class="support-prose-layout"><aside class="support-toc"><h2>MADE WITH CARE</h2><nav aria-label="About our approach"><a href="#collection">About the collection</a><a href="#your-space">Your creative space</a><a href="#everyone">Room for different creators</a></nav></aside><article class="support-prose"><section id="collection"><h2>Thoughtful files, honest descriptions</h2><p>Our collection includes AI-assisted illustrations prepared for JotColoring. We aim to describe what a page shows, keep uncolored files clean, and make download choices understandable. Colored examples are demonstrations; they do not change the original outline.</p><p>AI-assisted work can have imperfections, and no collection is a promise of exclusive rights in every element. If you spot an error in a page or description, send us the page link so it can be reviewed.</p></section><section id="your-space"><h2>Your work stays close</h2><p>Studio artwork and boards are saved in your browser on this device. They are not automatically published or synchronized. You decide when to export or share. Keep an editable backup if you want to move a project or protect it from cleared browser data.</p><a href="/privacy/">How your information is handled</a></section><section id="everyone"><h2>For a quick break or a longer project</h2><p>Choose an easy moment with color or spend time on the details. Print for a non-commercial class, explore an imaginative scene, or organize your favorite patterns. We want the interface to be welcoming on a phone and a desktop, with clear text, familiar controls and useful alternatives.</p><p>There are accessibility limits in visual canvas painting. We explain them openly and welcome feedback that helps improve the experience.</p><a href="/accessibility/">Read our accessibility approach</a></section></article></div>
</SupportShell>
